# Pre-specification

Answers to the pre-analysis form. Closed answers are shown in English; open
answers are quoted verbatim, in the client's language ({{ language }}).
{% for section in sections %}

## {{ section.title }}
{% for field in section.fields %}

### {{ field.title }}

{% if not field.answer %}
Not provided.
{% elif field.answer.quote %}
{{ field.answer.quote | quote }}
{% elif field.answer.list %}
{% for item in field.answer.list %}
- {{ item }}
{% endfor %}
{% else %}
{{ field.answer.text }}
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
{% endfor %}

## Open points

{% if open_points.length %}
{% for point in open_points %}
- {{ point }}
{% endfor %}
{% else %}
None.
{% endif %}
{#
  (This comment is at the bottom because the file has to begin with `---`:
  anything before it, an empty line included, and the front matter is gone.)

  The pre-specification: the form's answers as a markdown document.
  Rendered by `src/prespec.js` with an environment with no autoescape (it is
  markdown, not HTML): the client's text comes in **only** through the `quote`
  filter. Why it is made this way: see the comment at the top of
  `src/prespec.js`.

  DO NOT EDIT THE COPY INSIDE A SUBSYSTEM.
  This file says what **shape** the pre-specification has, so it is
  configuration: the original is in
  `webtools/configurator/documents/prespec.md.njk` and the copies
  (`preanalyst/templates/commons/`) are distributed by
  `webtools/configurator/documents_deployer/deploy.sh`.

  A limit: the template is coupled to `src/prespec.js`, which passes it the
  variables. The document's shape can be changed, but fields the code does not
  send cannot be invented.
#}